    "limitations": [
      "Reference date is 31 December 2025 (Stichtag of A I 17 – j / 25, published July 2026). berlin_population refers to 30 June 2026; any combination must show both reference periods. Household counts are households, not persons, and are never current population.",
      "Households are register-generated 'Wohnhaushalte' (HHGen procedure on the Berlin population register, main residence), not surveyed households. The publisher states the method overstates single-person households; persons in institutions are excluded. Figures are not comparable with Mikrozensus or Zensus household counts.",
      "'Children' are unmarried persons under 18 without own children or own household. Households in which all children are 18 or older count as households without children ('sonstige Mehrpersonenhaushalte ohne Kind').",
      "households_with_children_share is derived as 100 × households_with_children / households_total from worksheet T4 (same table, same date), rounded to 2 decimals; it is null when either input is not observed and not_applicable when there are no households. single_parent_share_of_households_with_children is published by the source (T4 column I) with denominator households_with_children.",
      "residents_in_households_total counts persons in private households (T1.1) and differs from the berlin_population total by date and by excluding institutional population; do not substitute one for the other.",
      "Tables overlap by design (size, type, children, single-person age): metrics from different breakdowns and totals with their components must not be added together. Single-person age bands use an exclusive upper bound.",
      "The workbook's code directory (worksheet Schlüssel) is dated December 2024 and uses the 2021 LOR scheme (542 Planungsräume); codes are joined exactly to the pinned berlin_lor snapshot. Code compatibility does not certify unchanged polygon boundaries.",
      "Source access, worksheet mappings, legend and CC BY 3.0 DE license (Impressum worksheet) checked 2026-10-18. Legend markers are kept as quality flags; '/' (not reliable enough) and '•' (unknown or confidential) are stored as suppressed nulls, '–' as zero; other annotations (p, r, s, parentheses) fail the import rather than being guessed."
